tags: disk, disk space, root filesystem

The disk of one instance: the size of the block device that holds its root filesystem.
It includes the files of the service and the free space for writes. It is a total, not
the free space.

The value is in bytes. Example: 1073741824 (1 GiB). With the setting read_mode=ro, the
device holds only the files of the service, and the value is the most that they can
use.

An absent value says nothing (it is not 0). Valid in the resources of a container. The
node reserves the value and charges for it. The processes cannot write more than the
device holds.

=== formal
class=resource
measure=the size of the block device that holds the root filesystem of the instance: the files of the service and the free space for writes, as a total
